# Task 4 review — evaluator truth

## Spec Compliance

The V5-only evidence envelope is isolated on `SimulationResultV5` at
`core/backtest_engine.py:747-754`; legacy `SimulationResult` is unchanged. Entries
create immutable quantity evidence at `core/backtest_engine.py:4220-4244`; all normal,
gap-stop, intraday-stop, policy, eviction, and terminal close routes converge through
`_close_trade`/`_finalize_v5_position_episode` at `core/backtest_engine.py:4180-4186`,
`4666-4701`, `4740-4774`, and `5055-5259`. Completed-bar extrema are updated only in
the after-close V5 phase (`4776-4803`), with high used for maxima and low for minima
(`5191-5222`), so opening/intraday exits do not consume an incomplete bar.

Checkpoints carry completed/open episode evidence, observations, fill totals, and policy
counts (`core/backtest_engine.py:2580-2638`, `3387-3417`); state-log recovery rewrites
the terminal observation (`1793-1861`). `summarize_panel_result` is the functional
report builder and validates panel/equity/benchmark/observation/fill/episode/policy
evidence before reporting (`core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py:614-860`). The unchanged
Task-3 evaluator call site accepts the exact keyword interface
(`core/pit_optimizer_v5/evaluator.py:47-55`, `418-422`).

Role evidence uses stable IDs, only aggregate candidates, and validates both the 96-item
and serialized 16-KiB bounds for every tentative projection
(`core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py:862-955`,
`core/pit_optimizer_v5/contracts.py:530-602`). Source identity requires the closed
source map and now includes diagnostics (`core/pit_optimizer_v5/contracts.py:24-46`,
`149-189`).

## Strengths

- Report construction fail-closes on curve/session, terminal-cash, fill-friction,
  episode/trade, entry-outcome, and policy-outcome mismatches
  (`core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py:123-380`, `614-650`). Net remains the report's
  portfolio metric while gross is a cost-add-back diagnostic (`651-665`, `826-835`).
- Zero-observation trade metrics are explicitly `None`, while cash drag remains an
  honest zero when there is no invested sleeve (`693-715`, `745-755`).
- Causal regime/year slices and month-end rolling windows are derived from authenticated
  observations/sessions (`515-612`), and provider projection deliberately omits rolling
  end dates (`924-933`).

## Issues Critical

None.

## Issues Important

- `core/pit_optimizer_v5/diagnostics.py:361-371` — `_validate_episodes` checks only
  that a quantity path starts with `entry`, ends at zero, has the declared add-on count,
  and uses panel sessions. It does not reconcile each quantity-path transition's
  action, session, execution price, or before/after quantity to the corresponding
  `EpisodeId` fill rows. The preceding aggregate buy/sell checks (`343-359`) therefore
  allow a checkpoint/result with a fabricated scale-out or add-on path to produce a
  report, despite mismatched fill evidence. This violates the required fail-closed
  reconciliation of quantity paths. Reconstruct the cumulative position quantity from
  fills in chronological order and require a one-for-one match with every path entry
  (including action/session/execution price), rejecting any mismatch. Confidence: 9/10.

## Issues Minor

None.

## Assessment

**DONE_WITH_CONCERNS.** The implementation covers the requested V5 causal evidence,
close-path finalization, checkpoint preservation, reconciled reporting, source identity,
and bounded aggregate role projection. Address the quantity-path-to-fill reconciliation
gap before treating the report as fully fail-closed.
